# The AUR repository tracks the packaging sources and nothing else: no built
# package, no filelist, no src/ or pkg/ directory. Everything is ignored and
# the tracked files are force-added (git add -f), which is what the AUR
# submission guidelines suggest for keeping the working tree clean.
#
# In this repository this file is called aur.gitignore. A file named
# .gitignore here would ignore this directory in md-notes itself; the
# publish-aur workflow copies it into the AUR checkout under its real name.
*
